{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26277 - PROTEIN:5793",
  "verbalization": "Stecholide I is implicated in the regulation of a sialyltransferase enzyme, CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme in the synthesis of sialic acid. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including Leosibirone B and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, all of which are linked to the hepatocyte. The evidence suggests that Stecholide I may exert its biological effects through a mechanism that involves the inhibition or modulation of this sialyltransferase, ultimately leading to a functional impact on hepatocytes. The consistent targeting of this enzyme by multiple compounds, along with the direct interaction with hepatocytes, supports a plausible mechanism by which Stecholide I could influence cellular processes in liver cells. The observed scores and the shared target relationship across the three paths indicate a robust and well-supported pathway, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
